{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Pushed as Gerrit change 3065: commit ad630728043, rebased onto S8 (2ece4c6b312, now origin/main). The rebase had 14 conflicts:\n- import lines in 12 files: kept the scratch_retention import and the typed-payload imports, and dropped the deleted `summary_route` import;\n- the CHANGELOG.md and release-notes.md entries: all of them are kept, and each was checked to match the commit it came from.\n\n`make verify` on the rebased tree exited 0 (19712 passed, 86 skipped). The pre-rebase run also exited 0 (19701 passed).\n\nThe diff is 87 files (1343 insertions, 4642 deletions). The only file outside the declared impact is `CHANGELOG.md` (the BREAKING entry).\n\nAC evidence:\n- the 5 modules are gone from the tree;\n- `len(_VALID_COMBINATIONS) == 10 == set(_LEAVES)`, pinned in `test_mutation.py` and `test_outbound_pass_typed_payload_cutover.py`;\n- `outbound_fields.py` is 192 LOC, and its only function is `_map_local_to_jira_fields`;\n- the Testing-section grep over src is empty.\n\nSizes: `applier.py` 759 LOC, `batch_dispatch.py` 729.\n\nRatchets:\n- complexity `new=0 increased=0`; `_diff_fields` and `applier.apply` are now stale;\n- mechanism `--update-stale` dropped `env_var::REBAR_RECONCILER_VERBOSE` and the `test_dc_summary_executor.py` autouse fixture;\n- the env registry now has 148 variables, and the `test_gen_env_registry.py` floor is 148.\n\nDeviations from the plan:\n1. `_build_leaves` raises `RuntimeError` instead of using `assert`, so the check survives `python -O`.\n2. The batch form validates the whole batch before the mode-cap split, so a plain-dict create fails before any inbound write.\n3. `test_summary_asymmetry_never_suppressed` is deleted. It pinned dead `_diff_fields` behaviour that the live diff contradicts, and live title-sync coverage is in `test_inbound_field_sync_directionality.py`.\n4. The manifest and preview tests now expect the typed payload's dict form.\n\nNot run: 2 external tests that build plain-dict payloads but do not go through the batch form (`test_link_sync_roundtrip_live.py`, `test_cloud_coordinator_lifecycle.py`). External tests are not part of `make verify`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792649009378240943,"uuid":"a63d2e35-f5c2-4d43-bc9a-a39454ffb9f7"}